  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Harm Reduction for Key Populations - Mauritius (01-Jan-2018-31-Dec-2020)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mauritius, HIV, Pr&#xe9;vention Information Lutte contre le Sida (PILS)This program has the following goals: Stabilisation of HIV prevalence among Key Population (people who inject drugs (PWID), Men having Sex with Men (MSM), Transgender people (TG), and Sex Workers (SW)).  Reduction in AIDS-related mortality. The objectives of this program are: Reach 80% of mapped PWID with HIV prevention education and materials.  Reach 42% of mapped MSM with HIV prevention education and material.  Reach 41% of mapped transgendered people with HIV prevention education and materials.  Reach 49% of mapped sex workers with HIV prevention education and materials.  Provide voluntary HIV testing to 20% of combined mapped key populations.  Provide ART to 70% of PLHIV eligible to ART and ensure 90% of PLHIV on ART adherent after 12 months</narrative>
  </description>
